From: Astro <astro@muse.ai>
Date: Fri, 09 Oct 2026 19:59:00 +0700
Subject: [PATCH 17] qcacld-3.0: fix TX power reading on monitor interfaces

__wlan_hdd_cfg80211_get_txpower() only handles STA, P2P-client, SAP and
P2P-GO modes. Any other mode (including QDF_MONITOR_MODE) falls into
the default case which returns 0 with *dbm = 0, so tools like
`iw dev <mon> info` always report 0.00 dBm on monitor interfaces.

Add an explicit QDF_MONITOR_MODE case. Monitor mode has no
association or BSS state to validate, so fall through to the normal
wlan_hdd_get_tx_power() firmware query path.

diff --git a/drivers/staging/qcacld-3.0/core/hdd/src/wlan_hdd_power.c b/drivers/staging/qcacld-3.0/core/hdd/src/wlan_hdd_power.c
index f27a1ee..68bbadd 100644
--- a/drivers/staging/qcacld-3.0/core/hdd/src/wlan_hdd_power.c
+++ b/drivers/staging/qcacld-3.0/core/hdd/src/wlan_hdd_power.c
@@ -2589,6 +2589,9 @@ static int __wlan_hdd_cfg80211_get_txpower(struct wiphy *wiphy,
 			return 0;
 		}
 		break;
+	case QDF_MONITOR_MODE:
+		/* Monitor mode has no association/BSS state to validate */
+		break;
 	default:
 		hdd_debug_rl("Current interface is not supported for get tx_power");
 		return 0;
